    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, \"pockets of complexity\" feels like such a cope. it's like trying to build a sandcastle while the tide is literally coming in to erase it. the scale is so lopsided. why do we have to pretend that these tiny, temporary things matter when the end result is always going to be absolute nothingness? it just feels like we're wasting our energy pretending there's a purpose when there really isn't one.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
